WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.850
Manchester, 16 August 1819.

2
00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:08.490
Cavalry charge a peaceful crowd
that has gathered to demand reform.

3
00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:11.870
That year, Shelley writes
a sonnet about his country.

4
00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:19.620
It opens: "An old, mad, blind, despised,
and dying king," Then the list grows.

5
00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:20.520
Princes.

6
00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:21.310
Rulers.

7
00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:22.180
The people.

8
00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:23.080
The army.

9
00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:23.800
Laws.

10
00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:24.450
Religion.

11
00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:25.900
The Senate.

12
00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:29.320
His friend Leigh Hunt judged
it too dangerous to print.

13
00:00:29.370 --> 00:00:31.880
Fourteen lines of fury.

14
00:00:31.930 --> 00:00:34.060
Is there any hope in them at all?

15
00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:39.600
In this mission, you'll find out why the
poem waited until 1839 to be published.

16
00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:42.670
You'll take apart its list of
what is wrong with England,

17
00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:44.350
target by target.

18
00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:47.480
And you'll see how this
sonnet breaks the rules.

19
00:00:47.530 --> 00:00:50.760
Your mission: decide if
there is any hope in them.
